    "updated_at": "2018-05-16T07:25:04Z",
    "body": "That's what I was thinking too. My thoughts were that we sorta get this for free with the fact that:\r\n\r\n - Just about everything in the script fetching language supports the existence and down-stream communication of the referrer policy member of a script fetch options struct (we just currently don't setup a top-level script to recognize the policy via the attribute this PR adds)\r\n - [HostImportModuleDynamically](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#hostimportmoduledynamically(referencingscriptormodule,-specifier,-promisecapability)), in Step 3, sets options to [descendent script fetch options](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#descendant-script-fetch-options) which should communicate a referrer policy down-stream effectively as needed\r\n\r\nI'm not sure about static imports or how that is spec'ed/differs in spec from dynamic imports, but I'm thinking we get this sorta stuff out of the box?",
